Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:05:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): add containment episode reducer and local
 storage fences [daveey]

Keep containment as an unreleased episode set, independent of insertion order or generic lifecycle events. Require explicit authenticated-release verification; reject stale predicate hashes and reused producer run/event identities. Add opt-in local task/history/edge fences with transaction- and task-scoped writer permits. These seams are not installed by normal connections: lifecycle, Board/courier and durable canonical-release verification remain prerequisites before activation.

Proof: canonical scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_containment_state.py tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_containment_policy.py tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_containment_legacy_paths.py: 115 passed, 0 failed. scripts/check --base origin/main passed. Local fence tests preserve the relay consumer edge and reject status/history/edge writes across new SQLite connections; not a deployed CLI/tool containment claim.
